Subject: ppu_lifter: jump-table detection window stops at the previous block end

discover_jump_tables() looks at the 30 instructions before each bctr to decide
whether the table holds offsets (an `add rC,rC,base` feeds mtctr) and how many
entries it has (a `cmplwi idx,N`). That window is fixed and crosses function and
block boundaries. With two neighbouring switch functions -- an offset table, then
an absolute table -- the absolute one picked up the previous function's `add`,
was decoded as offsets (every target outside .text), and its bctr lifted to an
unresolved indirect call.

Found by recomp_android's PPU differential test (tests/ps3/ppu_diff, flow suite).
Base: sp00nznet/ps3recomp 39a36296511c445707adabcd312f0b740cfbd694.

--- a/tools/ppu_lifter.py	2026-10-17 21:37:40.209619420 +0000
+++ b/tools/ppu_lifter.py	2026-10-17 21:37:40.223695961 +0000
@@ -4317,6 +4317,16 @@
             continue
         _dbg(all_insns[i].addr, "bctr found")
         win = all_insns[max(0, i - 30):i]
+        # The fixed 30-instruction window can reach back across the previous function (or an
+        # earlier block that ends in blr/bctr/b): an `add rC,rC,base` or a `cmplwi` found there
+        # belongs to someone else's switch. Two neighbouring switches -- one offset table, one
+        # absolute -- made the absolute one decode as offsets (every target out of range) and
+        # its bctr lift to an unresolved indirect call. Keep only the run that can fall into
+        # this bctr.
+        for _k in range(len(win) - 1, -1, -1):
+            if win[_k].mnemonic in ('blr', 'bctr', 'b', 'ba'):
+                win = win[_k + 1:]
+                break
         win_cand = _live(_scan_lo(i), i)
         # the ctr source register (last mtctr before the bctr)
         rC = None
